{"step_index":909,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:30:48Z","thinking":"**Investigating inductive hypothesis generalization**\n\nThe inductive hypothesis `ih`'s type depends on `h` because `h` was in scope when `induction d` was invoked. The `induction d` tactic generalizes hypotheses involving variables or `d` as arguments. The `obtain` statement left `h : k ≤ k + d` in the context, and thus `induction d` generalized it. To prevent this generalization, either `clear h` prior to `induction d` or use the `induction d with ...` syntax.\n\n\n**Analyzing walk and ballWithin definitions**\n\n`clear h` eliminates the hypothesis generalization issue. Now considering `mem_ballWithin_of_walk`. Examining `Walk.cons`, the edge is added at the beginning of the walk, not the end. The inductive definition of `Walk` suggests an approach utilizing induction on walk length. The goal is to relate reachability in a walk to set membership in `ballWithin`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python3 -c '\\nimport subprocess\\nlean_cmd = [\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh\\\", \\\"scratch.lean\\\"]\\n'\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Testing check\"","toolSummary":"\"Check test\""}}]}
